From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, winex11: the default keyboard layout is the session's keyboard (9901)

On Windows the default input layout (Preload) is the one the person types
with, and an HKL names both halves: the input language in its low word,
the keyboard layout in its high word -- an English (US) session typing
with a German keyboard is 0x04070409, with US Dvorak 0xf0020409. Wine made
both halves the user locale's whatever the X keyboard map was, and
answered that HKL from the X map: on a German map in an English (US)
session GetKeyboardLayout said US English (0x04090409, "00000409"), and a
program that loaded or activated US English (games and emulators do, for
predictable keys) still got German answers from MapVirtualKeyEx,
VkKeyScanEx and ToUnicodeEx. A Dvorak map reported US and US answered as
Dvorak (KBD-HKL's open end: "variant X maps report the language HKL").

The display driver now says which Windows layout its keyboard map is (new
user driver entry GetKeyboardLayoutDevice): winex11 matches the X map's
XKB layout and variant against its tables -- the layout-id KLIDs of 8212
(us(dvorak) is 00010409, Layout Id 0002), then the languages with that XKB
name (the user locale's own first, so "us" stays en-AU in an en-AU
session), then those with that XKB layout and no variant (de(nodeadkeys)
is German). win32u's default layout takes that as its high word; an X
map no Windows layout has (epo) and the Wayland driver keep the locale's
HKL. Asking loads the display driver, as MapVirtualKeyEx does, except
while sysparams_init writes Preload at every process start (it keeps the
locale's name there, and the thread asks again afterwards). winex11 answers
the X map's own HKL from the X map and, when it knows it, builds every
other layout from XKB -- including the locale's HKL when the map is not
that layout -- so US English on a German map is US, as on Windows. The
low word stays the locale's, so the language programs see is unchanged;
an X map that is the locale's layout (the usual case) gives the same HKL
as before.
Gate: test/kbddevice-gate.sh; mutant SG_MUTANT_KBD_LOCALE_DEVICE.
---
